## 2.5.4 (Released 2025-09-21) {#2.5.4}

### User notes {#2.5.4-user-notes}

<div class="changelog-entry">

You can now add notes for a user in the usercard by clicking on the "Add notes" button. Notes are saved globally per user.

{{ figure("/img/changelog/2.5.4/usercard-notes.png") }}

{{ credit(author="fourtf, pajlada", helper="isgkm, Nerixyz", prs="6122, 6318, 6413") }}

</div>

### Usercard indicators {#2.5.4-usercard-indicators}

<div class="changelog-entry">

When a user is live, the usercard will now show a red dot next to their name. Hovering over it will reveal the number of viewers.

{{ figure("/img/changelog/2.5.4/usercard-live-indicator.png") }}

{{ credit(author="Nerixyz", prs="6383") }}

The "Created" and "Following since" dates now have a tooltip that shows the duration since that event.

{{ figure("/img/changelog/2.5.4/usercard-following-since-tooltip.png") }}

{{ credit(author="Nerixyz", helper="pajlada", prs="6384") }}

</div>

### Duplicate messages {#2.5.4-duplicate-messages}

<div class="changelog-entry">

The "Allow sending duplicate messages" setting now works again.

{{ credit(author="brian6932", helper="tetyys, Nerixyz, pajlada, jupjohn, Mm2PL", prs="6417") }}

The "Allow sending duplicate messages" setting now works again.

{{ credit(author="brian6932", helper="tetyys, Nerixyz, pajlada, jupjohn, Mm2PL", prs="6417") }}

</div>

### Chat input {#2.5.4-chat-input}

<div class="changelog-entry">

When colon-completing emotes in chat, you can now use `:~` to filter for zero-width emotes.

{{ figure("/img/changelog/2.5.4/colon-tilde-complete.png", width=300, caption="Colon completing only zero-width emotes") }}

{{ credit(author="droidicus", helper="pajlada, Nerixyz", prs="6362, 6440") }}

In fast chats, you might not notice that your message was successfully sent.
Chatterino can now pulse the text input when your messages have been received
in chat. You can enable this feature by enabling the "Pulse text input when
one of your messages is successfully sent" setting.

{{ figure("/img/changelog/2.5.4/chatinput-pulse.webm", width=350) }}

{{ credit(author="pajlada", prs="6380") }}

</div>

### Chat window {#2.5.4-chat-window}

<div class="changelog-entry">

You can now disable the reduced opacity for historical messages.

<div class="figure-group">
  {{ figure("/img/changelog/2.5.4/historic-opacity-default.png", width=406, caption="The default look") }}
  {{ figure("/img/changelog/2.5.4/historic-opacity-disabled.png", width=406, caption="With the setting disabled") }}
</div>
{{ credit(author="fourtf", helper="Mm2PL", prs="6121") }}

Chatterino now supports emojis from Unicode 16.0.

<i>Editor's note: it seems like these are not available on Twitch right now.</i>
{{ credit(author="Nerixyz", prs="6155") }}

</div>

### Logging {#2.5.4-logging}

<div class="changelog-entry">

The timestamp used in the logs is now customizable, similar to the one used in the app itself.

{{ credit(author="droidicus", helper="Nerixyz, pajlada", prs="6338") }}

Logs can now use the timestamp of messages provided by Twitch instead of the
local one. This behaviour is disabled by default.

{{ credit(author="droidicus", helper="Nerixyz, pajlada", prs="6346") }}

</div>

### Image Uploader {#2.5.4-image-uploader}

<div class="changelog-entry">

Chatterino can now export and import the image uploader configuration to/from the clipboard.
The import also supports a subset of the format used by the ShareX application.

{{ credit(author="knobby-tires, x3rt", helper="pajlada, Nerixyz", prs="6284, 6387, 6394") }}

For image upload services that serve the response in an array, the JSON selector can now query arrays using their indices like `foo.0`.

{{ credit(author="Nerixyz", prs="6193") }}

</div>

