### Plugins {#2.5.4-plugins}

<div class="changelog-entry">

Through `c2.WebSocket`, plugins can now open WebSocket connections. This can be used to listen to events from third party services.

{{ credit(author="Nerixyz", helper="Mm2PL, pajlada", prs="6076, 6141, 6186, 6314, 6315") }}

Plugins can now create styled messages through `c2.Message.new()`.
Previously, only system (gray) messages could be created.
Compared to C++, there are a few capabilities missing&mdash;namely emotes and images.
These will be added in future releases along with an API to inspect and alter existing messages (e.g. in filters).

{{ credit(author="Nerixyz", helper="Mm2PL, pajlada", prs="5754") }}

For plugin developers, there is a new REPL (read-eval-print-loop) window similar to the browser console.
It displays log messages and allows you to evaluate Lua code in the context of the plugin.
You have to manually enable this in your [`settings.json`](https://wiki.chatterino.com/Settings/) where you have to set `plugins.repl.enabled` to `true` and restart. Then you can open the REPL from the plugin settings.

{{ figure("/img/changelog/2.5.4/plugin-repl.png", width=400, caption="Plugin REPL showing the new message API.") }}

{{ credit(author="Nerixyz", helper="Mm2PL, pajlada", prs="6120") }}

If you have ideas for plugins, check out [this discussion](https://github.com/Chatterino/chatterino2/discussions/4999).

You can find technical documentation for plugins
[here](https://github.com/Chatterino/chatterino2/blob/4927ad8bb7b1db86c28566623eafcd0009734794/docs/wip-plugins.md).

</div>

### Crash fixes {#2.5.4-crash-fixes}

<div class="changelog-entry">

Fixes various crashes that could occur when:

- shutting down Chatterino (either at the wrong time, or just at all)
- running Chatterino attached to a conhost that was closed before Chatterino
- EventSub had connection issues
- searching in an emote popup that was started from a non-Twitch channel
- plugins would make an HTTP request from a timeout handler

{{ credit(author="pajlada, vincent0955, Nerixyz", helper="Leppunen, brian6932", prs="6187,
	6197, 6161, 6204, 6213, 6368, 6357, 6375") }}

</div>

### Miscellaneous changes {#2.5.4-miscellaneous-changes}

<div class="changelog-entry">

- The paused indicator is now more visible and easier to notice. {{ credit(author="jacob-thompson", helper="pajlada, Nerixyz, iProdigy", prs="6123", inline=true) }}

- In addition to the existing options like opening a split, you can now open a channel in a custom player when right-clicking on a twitch.tv link. {{ credit(author="brian6932", prs="6403", inline=true) }}

- The emote and badge size can now be changed independently of Chatterino's overall scale. {{ credit(author="4rneee", helper="pajlada", prs="6126", inline=true) }}

- Chatterino now saves the emotes from third party providers and loads these if they fail to load upon restarting the app. {{ credit(author="occluder", helper="pajlada, Mm2PL, Nerixyz", prs="6125, 6229", inline=true) }}

- Message character length label font is now monospaced, meaning the message input box should jump around a little bit less. {{ credit(author="pajlada", prs="6366", inline=true) }}

- Popup overlay now only draws an outline when being interacted with. {{ credit(author="teknsl", prs="6140", inline=true) }}

- You can now disable the "double-click tab to rename" behaviour. {{ credit(author="jupjohn", prs="6163, 6184", inline=true) }}

- In the settings dialog, you can now search for filters, nicknames, and commands from the top bar. {{ credit(author="apa420", prs="5886, 5890, 5891", inline=true) }}

- You can now add a custom hotkey for opening the account selector. {{ credit(author="teknsl", prs="6192", inline=true) }}

- On Linux, you can now set the window background to a transparent color. {{ credit(author="apa420", prs="6137", inline=true) }}

</div>

